{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(12) \\\\ 16 & =48p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{1}{3}$ is positive." 13194139533931 true] [17592186096918 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533931 true] [17592186096918 1145 "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-12,6),$ we can substitute $x=-12$ and $y=6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(-12) \\\\ 36 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266659 1017 #edb/ref 17592186266660 13194139533931 true] [17592186266659 1089 "q-115625" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266659 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533931 true] [17592186266659 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/b14a6063e0b1be751e738060087644cacaa3c3cf1e324ee66bf57232834e618d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266659 1113 #uuid "1dea1f83-fad7-5576-8d47-906556eb6e45" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266659 1145 "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-1,1).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-1,1),$ we can substitute $x=-1$ and $y=1$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {1}^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 1 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is negative." 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266661 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266662 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266663 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266664 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266665 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1041 "selection" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266665 13194139533931 true] [17592186266660 1110 #uuid "a0ccf9bd-7fb1-568b-ad99-4cfc3bfd80ec" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266661 1034 "{y}^{2}=4x" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533931 true] [17592186266661 1111 #uuid "67bbc023-ac58-5171-908d-2badfbe1d3a3" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266662 1034 "{y}^{2}=x" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533931 true] [17592186266662 1111 #uuid "63d16d93-ebd9-50d6-8243-2b7d9b616fa3" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266663 1034 "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}x" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533931 true] [17592186266663 1111 #uuid "ff3afbb8-119f-511b-a599-963062379f97" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266664 1034 "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}x" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266664 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533931 true] [17592186266664 1111 #uuid "e257f06d-b2af-57e0-974c-daae06b1d9f7" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266665 1034 "{y}^{2}=-x" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139