en parabola passes through the point $(6,-3),$ so we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3) \\\\ (-3-3)^{2} & =4p(6-3) \\\\ 36 & =12p \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3) \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =4(3)(x-3) \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =12(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=3$ is positive." 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266689 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266690 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266691 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266692 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266693 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1041 "selection" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266693 13194139533931 true] [17592186266688 1110 #uuid "094bad5d-3056-51a0-b6a9-d51a378c2415" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266689 1034 "(y-3)^{2}=-\\frac{3}{8}(x-3)" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533931 true] [17592186266689 1111 #uuid "2a282ecd-9120-5164-9142-e8fed956f6fb" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266690 1034 "(y+3)^{2}=3(x+3)" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533931 true] [17592186266690 1111 #uuid "01480733-3dea-5b7a-a998-8e6987364ac0" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266691 1034 "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}(x+3)" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266691 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533931 true] [17592186266691 1111 #uuid "90da7ecc-92e5-566f-b1ae-aa71cd79d6d4" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266692 1034 "(x-3)^{2}=-12(y-3)" 13194139533931 true] [17592186266692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533931 true] [17592186266692 1111 #uuid "6faf3cff-1208-501c-bd13-4ddc53d72dba" 13194139533931 true] [175921862